      "id": "9e6db39d-2f57-4b1e-9c8a-f4cb6585176f",
      "name": "Execute: Check Availability",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflow",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        -820,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Same decision structure as 14's scheduling branch (propose / confirm / clarify), reworded for text messages.\nconst trigger = $('When Executed by Another Workflow').first().json;\nconst availability = $('Execute: Check Availability').first().json;\nconst slots = availability.available_slots || [];\n\nlet history = '';\ntry {\n  const messages = $('Get Recent Messages').all().map(item => item.json);\n  if (messages.length > 0) history = messages.map(m => `${m.role}: ${m.content}`).join('\\n\\n');\n} catch (e) { /* first message in the conversation */ }\n\nconst slotsText = slots.length > 0\n  ? slots.slice(0, 8).map(s => `- ${s.starts_at} to ${s.ends_at}`).join('\\n')\n  : 'No open slots found in the checked date range.';\n\nconst prompt = `You are handling a scheduling request that arrived over WhatsApp for a real estate agency.\n\n${history ? `Recent conversation history:\\n${history}\\n\\n` : 'This is the first message in the conversation.\\n\\n'}New WhatsApp message:\n${trigger.body}\n\nCurrently available viewing slots (UTC):\n${slotsText}\n\nDecide one of three things:\n1. \"propose\" -- the customer is asking about availability but hasn't confirmed a specific time yet. Draft a short reply listing 3-4 of the available slots above in a natural, readable way, asking them to pick one.\n2. \"confirm\" -- the customer's message clearly confirms one specific time that was previously offered AND that time is still in the available slots list above. Draft a reply confirming it's noted and the team will finalize it shortly. Extract the exact starts_at and ends_at (ISO 8601 UTC) for the confirmed slot.\n3. \"clarify\" -- ambiguous, or they referenced a time NOT in the available slots list. Draft a reply asking them to confirm which listed time works, or to pick a different one.\n\nRespond with ONLY strict JSON: { \"action\": \"propose\"|\"confirm\"|\"clarify\", \"draft_body\": \"...\", \"confirmed_slot\": { \"starts_at\": \"...\", \"ends_at\": \"...\" } | null }`;\n\nreturn [{ json: { ...trigger, prompt } }];"
      },
      "id": "378cfdd9-96be-46dc-8d86-bf75e5351363",
      "name": "Build Scheduling Prompt",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -560,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages",
        "authentication": "predefinedCredentialType",
        "nodeCredentialType": "anthropicApi",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "anthropic-version",
              "value": "2023-06-01"
            },
            {
              "name": "content-type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ model: \"claude-sonnet-4-6\", max_tokens: 600, messages: [ { role: \"user\", content: $json.prompt } ] }) }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "eb8050b8-4604-4f53-81ef-571f997fc692",
      "name": "Call Claude (Scheduling)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.5,
      "position": [
        -300,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Identical logic to 14's \"Parse Scheduling Result\" -- only trust confirmed_slot when action === 'confirm'.\nlet raw = '';\ntry { raw = $json.content[0].text; } catch (e) { throw new Error('Unexpected Claude scheduling response shape: ' + JSON.stringify($json)); }\nconst cleaned = raw.replace(/```json|```/g, '').trim();\nlet parsed;\ntry { parsed = JSON.parse(cleaned); } catch (e) { throw new Error('Failed to parse scheduling JSON: ' + cleaned); }\nconst ALLOWED_ACTIONS = ['propose', 'confirm', 'clarify'];\nif (!ALLOWED_ACTIONS.includes(parsed.action)) parsed.action = 'clarify';\nconst proposedAppointment = parsed.action === 'confirm' && parsed.confirmed_slot\n  ? { starts_at: parsed.confirmed_slot.starts_at, ends_at: parsed.confirmed_slot.ends_at } : null;\nreturn [{ json: { content: [{ type: 'text', text: parsed.draft_body || '' }], proposed_appointment: proposedAppointment } }];"
      },
      "id": "9296884c-c377-4355-80e3-449b2eb7fa32",
      "name": "Parse Scheduling Result",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Same as 14's generic branch: always goes to human review, so placeholders are fine.\nconst d = $('When Executed by Another Workflow').first().json;\nconst prompt = `Draft a short, friendly WhatsApp reply on behalf of a real estate agency to the message below.\nThis draft will be reviewed by a human before sending, so it's OK to leave placeholders like [confirm availability] if specifics are unknown.\nKeep it conversational -- no email-style greeting or sign-off, no subject line.\nCategory: ${d.category}\n\nCustomer's WhatsApp message:\n${d.body}\n\nRespond with ONLY the message text, no JSON, no markdown.`;\nreturn [{ json: { ...d, prompt } }];"
      },
